Ben (devex): FYI — got pinged by a new user who couldn't get the JS SDK working in an ESM + edge setup. They used `require('redwood')` and got a runtime error.
Tom (sdk): can you paste the error?
Ben (devex): "Cannot use import statement outside a module" when deploying to Vercel Edge. Local Node (CJS) was fine. They also said TS types were missing for the edge bundle.
Maya (docs): ugh — our quickstart only shows `import Redwood from 'redwood'` (ESM). We never have an explicit CJS example.
Tom (sdk): Right now pkg ships dual entrypoints but the docs don't show the mapping. Also we expose a default export which can be awkward in CJS land (you end up doing `const r = require('redwood').default || require('redwood')`).
Alice (edge-eng): Edge runtimes (Cloudflare/Vercel) require ESM. Bun/Deno also prefer ESM. We should show both forms and an explicit named export option: `export const createClient = ...` so people can do `import { createClient } from 'redwood'` which maps cleanly in both ESM and CJS (`const { createClient } = require('redwood')`).
Tom (sdk): We already have named exports for some helpers but not for the top-level default client factory. Small non-breaking change: add `export function createClient(...)` in the ESM build and ensure CJS build has `exports.createClient = createClient`.
Maya (docs): Good — from docs POV we should: 1) Add CJS snippet (Node <=14 or users using require) 2) Add Edge snippet showing `import { createClient } from 'redwood'` 3) Add a note about TypeScript `types` field and edge bundlers.
Ben (devex): Proposed doc snippets — please sanity-check: 
```js
// ESM / modern Node / Edge
import { createClient } from 'redwood';
const client = createClient({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_KEY });

// CJS / older Node
const { createClient } = require('redwood');
const client = createClient({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_KEY });
```
Tom (sdk): looks good. Also include this CJS fallback for folks stuck with default export: 
```js
// CJS fallback if someone used default export in older examples
const Redwood = require('redwood');
const createClient = Redwood.createClient || Redwood.default?.createClient || Redwood;
```
Maya (docs): For TS we should show typings: 
```ts
import { createClient, type ClientOptions } from 'redwood';
const client = createClient({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_KEY } as ClientOptions);
```
Alice (edge-eng): Add a short note: "Edge runtimes are ESM-only — use `import` and named exports. If using a bundler, ensure `target: 'esnext'` and keep the SDK as an external if you import server-side." :warning:
Ben (devex): Can we also add a tiny sample repo (edge-example) in the quickstarts repo that shows deployment to Vercel Edge + Typescript? That was the onboarding friction here.
Tom (sdk): I can open a PR to add `createClient` named export and update package.json fields (`module`, `main`, `exports`) to be explicit. Will also add a small note in CHANGELOG about compatibility.
Maya (docs): I'll draft the docs change after Tom's PR. Add a short FAQ entry: "Why am I seeing default export errors in Edge?" with the snip above.
deploy-bot: Deployed docs staging site for preview: https://staging.docs.redwood.ai/edge-imports :rocket:
Ben (devex): Awesome. Thanks all — let's keep this short and add the quickstart example within the week. :thumbsup:
